== planner_node_3  (runtime_class=bounded_transform) ==
  semantic_goal     : Analyze master data, inventory, consumption, demand signals, and lead times to assess inventory risk
  inputs.required   : 1
      - parsed_datasets          kind=dataset_collection src=planner_node_2
        schema_hint: ['sku_master', 'inventory_rt', 'demand_history_120d', 'market_signals', 'real_time_events', 'supplier_performance']
  output.primary    : inventory_risk_assessment kind=tabular_records   
        schema_hint: ['sku_id', 'warehouse', 'risk_score', 'risk_category', 'days_until_stockout', 'recommended_action']
  business_rules    : 4
      - [domain_policy] Risk score must be computed as a weighted combination of days_cover, criticality, supplier_reliability, and demand volatility.
      - [value_mapping] Risk category must be one of: 'critical', 'high', 'medium', 'low' based on risk score thresholds defined in business policy.
      - [data_integrity] Days until stockout must be calculated as available_qty / daily_demand_forecast, capped at 365.
  acceptance        : 6
      - [row_count] Output contains exactly one row per (sku_id, warehouse) combination present in inventory_rt.
      - [non_null] All rows have non-null values for sku_id, warehouse, risk_score, risk_category, days_until_stockout, recommended_action.
      - [enum_membership] risk_category values are one of: critical, high, medium, low.
  sketch            : 6 bullets
      • Extract the six datasets from the parsed_datasets collection (sku_master, inventory_rt, demand_history_120d, market_signals, real_time_events, supplier_performance).
      • Join inventory_rt with sku_master on sku_id to enrich with criticality, lead_time_days, target_service_level, base_daily_demand.
      • Compute daily demand forecast per (sku_id, warehouse) using demand_history_120d, market_signals, and real_time_events (e.g., moving average with seasonal adjustment).
      • Calculate days_cover = available_qty / daily_demand_forecast, then days_until_stockout = days_cover (capped at 365).
      • Compute risk_score as weighted combination of days_cover, criticality, supplier_reliability (from supplier_performance), and demand volatility; map to risk_category.
      • Derive recommended_action from risk_category and days_until_stockout, then output tabular records with the required schema.

== planner_node_4  (runtime_class=bounded_transform) ==
  semantic_goal     : Forecast future demand using historical consumption and market demand signals
  inputs.required   : 1
      - parsed_datasets          kind=dataset_collection src=planner_node_2
        schema_hint: ['sku_master', 'inventory_rt', 'demand_history_120d', 'market_signals', 'real_time_events', 'supplier_performance']
  output.primary    : demand_forecast          kind=tabular_records   
        schema_hint: ['sku_id', 'warehouse', 'forecast_date', 'forecast_qty', 'forecast_confidence_lower', 'forecast_confidence_upper']
  business_rules    : 4
      - [completeness] Forecast must be generated per (sku_id, warehouse) pair using at least 30 days of historical consumption data.
      - [domain_policy] Market demand signals (demand_index, maintenance_cycle_index, customer_backlog_index) must be incorporated as exogenous regressors in the forecast model.
      - [domain_policy] Forecast horizon must be at least the maximum supplier lead time for each SKU, capped at 90 days.
  acceptance        : 5
      - [tabular_contract] Output contains exactly the fields: sku_id, warehouse, forecast_date, forecast_qty, forecast_confidence_lower, forecast_confidence_upper.
      - [non_null] Every row has non-null sku_id, warehouse, forecast_date, forecast_qty.
      - [value_range] forecast_confidence_lower <= forecast_qty <= forecast_confidence_upper for every row.
  sketch            : 5 bullets
      • Load the parsed_datasets collection from upstream, extracting demand_history_120d and market_signals tables.
      • Merge demand_history_120d with market_signals on date/week_start and category to enrich historical consumption with market indices.
      • For each (sku_id, warehouse) group, fit a time series model (e.g., ARIMA or Prophet) using at least 30 days of actual_consumption_qty and exogenous regressors from market signals.
      • Generate daily forecasts for the required horizon (max lead time, capped at 90 days) with 95% confidence intervals.
      • Output the forecast as a tabular_records dataset with columns: sku_id, warehouse, forecast_date, forecast_qty, forecast_confidence_lower, forecast_confidence_upper.

== planner_node_5  (runtime_class=bounded_transform) ==
  semantic_goal     : Combine risk assessment and demand forecast to make replenishment decisions and produce a ranked queue
  inputs.required   : 2
      - inventory_risk_assessment kind=tabular_records    src=planner_node_3
        schema_hint: ['sku_id', 'warehouse', 'risk_score', 'risk_category', 'days_until_stockout', 'recommended_action']
      - demand_forecast          kind=tabular_records    src=planner_node_4
        schema_hint: ['sku_id', 'warehouse', 'forecast_date', 'forecast_qty', 'forecast_confidence_lower', 'forecast_confidence_upper']
  output.primary    : replenishment_queue      kind=tabular_records   
        schema_hint: ['sku_id', 'part_name', 'warehouse', 'category', 'criticality', 'current_available_qty', 'forecast_daily_demand', 'lead_time_days', 'reorder_point', 'reorder_qty', 'suggested_order_qty', 'supplier_id', 'priority_score', 'decision_reason']
        locator_hint: /Users/llk/agentsFactory/scenario_data/spare_parts/output/replenishment_queue.csv
  business_rules    : 4
      - [domain_policy] Replenishment decision must consider both inventory risk category and demand forecast to compute priority score.
      - [value_mapping] Suggested order quantity must respect MOQ and reorder multiple from SKU master data.
      - [domain_policy] Reorder point must be calculated as forecast daily demand multiplied by lead time days plus safety stock.
  acceptance        : 5
      - [tabular_contract] Output must contain all required fields: sku_id, part_name, warehouse, category, criticality, current_available_qty, forecast_daily_demand, lead_time_days, reorder_point, reorder_qty, suggested_order_qty, supplier_id, priority_score, decision_reason.
      - [non_null] Each row must have a non-null sku_id and warehouse.
      - [value_range] suggested_order_qty must be a non-negative integer.
  sketch            : 6 bullets
      • Load the inventory risk assessment dataset from planner_node_3.
      • Load the demand forecast dataset from planner_node_4.
      • Join both datasets on sku_id and warehouse to create a unified view per SKU-warehouse.
      • For each SKU-warehouse, compute reorder point, suggested order quantity (respecting MOQ and reorder multiple), and priority score based on risk category and forecast.
      • Generate a human-readable decision_reason for each row.
      • Write the resulting replenishment queue to the specified output CSV file.

